  "description": "UPALEE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: H3 O1 1+,C320 H424 Dy5 Mn7 N12 O49 1-,16(C3 H7 N1 O1),1.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4? (Mn) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.380-3.854 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.05-115.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [MnIII6MnIIDy5(3-8H)3(μ3-OH)8(dmf)8(MeCN)4(H2O)9](OH)3(H2O)1.5(dmf)16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 9 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
